+## Changed
+
+- `src/core/run/verify-log.ts` (new): `writeVerifyLog` writes a run's whole
+  output to the next free `.run/logs/<target>-<n>.log`, creates `.run/logs/`
+  and its `.gitignore` (`*\n`) when missing, and returns the change-folder
+  relative path.
+- `src/core/run/verify-excerpt.ts`: added `tailVerifyOutput`, which keeps a
+  short text exactly (trailing newline included), the last
+  `limits.markerOutputLines` lines of a longer text with each line cut to
+  `limits.markerLineChars` by the shared `cutLine`, and `''` for blank text.
+- `src/watcher/verify.ts`: `runVerificationGateResult` now writes the run's log
+  and appends `verify_ran` with `log` plus the tail as `output` only when that
+  tail is not blank, and returns `log`. The record path moved to
+  `src/watcher/record-verify.ts` to keep `verify.ts` under its 200-line budget;
+  the compat `runVerificationGate` keeps its old shape (omitting `log` when it
+  is null) and now carries `log` when a context ran.
+- `src/watcher/task-verify.ts`, `change-verify.ts`, `archive-verify.ts`,
+  `src/core/run/scope-regression-marker.ts`: every `verify_ran`-based marker
+  ends with `Full output: <log>` when the log is known and keeps the old event
+  wording otherwise. `archive-verify.ts` now builds its marker from
+  `runVerificationGateResult` and no longer reads its `verify_ran` line back.
+- `src/core/run/scope-hash.ts`: `StaleTaskAudit` gained `log?: string`.
+- `src/watcher/regression.ts`: the audit's `log` is taken from the gate, the
+  `regressed` event's `output` is `tailVerifyOutput(...)`, and `autoRecertify`
+  receives a gate result whose `output` is that tail.
+- `src/harness/types.ts`: `VerifyRanEventData` gained `log?: string`.
+- Tests: new `tests/verify-log.test.ts`; `tests/dead-marker-excerpt.test.ts`,
+  `tests/scope-regression-excerpt.test.ts`, `tests/verify-excerpt.test.ts`
+  updated to the log pointer and log-file reads; golden fixtures
+  `tests/fixtures/events/verified.jsonl` and `dead.jsonl` regenerated with
+  `UPDATE_GOLDEN=1`, differing only by the new `log` keys.
+
+The task verify command
+(`tests/verify-log.test.ts tests/dead-marker-excerpt.test.ts
+tests/scope-regression-excerpt.test.ts tests/verify-excerpt.test.ts
+tests/golden-events.test.ts tests/retry-prior-output.test.ts
+tests/osq-change-env.test.ts`) passes: 36/36. The CLI typecheck and biome pass.
+
+## Missing context
+
+The task scope omits `src/watcher/fingerprint.ts`, but the acceptance also
+requires "Every other existing test passes unchanged" and the proposal verify
+is `pnpm verify`, which runs `tests/auto-retry.test.ts` and
+`tests/steering-triggers.test.ts`. Those two tests assert that two identical
+deaths of one task share a dead-marker fingerprint and become `stuck: true`.
+Pointing a dead marker's `Full output:` line at a per-run log
+(`.run/logs/1-1.log` then `.run/logs/1-2.log`) makes the two marker bodies
+differ, so the fingerprint differs and `stuck` is never set:
+
+- `tests/auto-retry.test.ts:214` (`marks a task stuck after two identical
+  deaths with no third attempt`)
+- `tests/steering-triggers.test.ts:445` (`marks a second identical death stuck
+  and later cycles spawn nothing`)
+
+`fingerprint.ts` is not in the task scope
+(`src/watcher/*verify.ts` requires a `verify` path segment), so I could not
+normalize the new volatile log pointer there. The living and delta specs do not
+modify the "Dead marker fingerprint" requirement either.
+
+## Outside scope
+
+`src/watcher/fingerprint.ts` (`normalizeFailureBody`) does not normalize the
+`.run/logs/<target>-<n>.log` pointer. Both failing tests above stem only from
+this. The correct minimal fix is one replacement in `normalizeFailureBody`,
+e.g. `.replace(/\.run\/logs\/([^/\s]+)-\d+\.log/g, '.run/logs/$1-<n>.log')`,
+plus a "Dead marker fingerprint" scenario in the watcher-and-harness delta
+spec. I left the file untouched per the scope rule.
+
+## Blocked
+
+I need the task scope to include `src/watcher/fingerprint.ts` (and its
+watcher-and-harness delta scenario) so the log pointer can be normalized for
+fingerprinting. Everything else in the task is implemented and the task verify
+is green; with that one normalization the proposal verify should pass as well.
+
+## Next
+
+Add the log-pointer normalization to `normalizeFailureBody` in
+`src/watcher/fingerprint.ts`, rerun `pnpm verify`, then finish.
+
+Touched: src/core/run/verify-log.ts, src/core/run/verify-excerpt.ts, src/core/run/scope-hash.ts, src/core/run/scope-regression-marker.ts, src/watcher/verify.ts, src/watcher/record-verify.ts, src/watcher/task-verify.ts, src/watcher/change-verify.ts, src/watcher/archive-verify.ts, src/watcher/regression.ts, src/harness/types.ts, tests/verify-log.test.ts, tests/dead-marker-excerpt.test.ts, tests/scope-regression-excerpt.test.ts, tests/verify-excerpt.test.ts, tests/fixtures/events/verified.jsonl, tests/fixtures/events/dead.jsonl
